/E (Founder Arnaud Zannier describes his philosophy as "a more humble luxury," developed in deliberate contrast to replicable grand hotel concepts. His properties in Namibia, Cambodia, Vietnam, and rural France, share one structural feature: they are difficult to reach by design. Multi-stage logistics, unconventional locations, and the absence of conventional resort amenities are not operational constraints: they are the product. The friction of arrival filters the guest demographic before check-in occurs, and the isolation protects the experience for those who have made it through.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
