/T (Revenue management versus aspirational scarcity.)
/E (Revenue management versus aspirational scarcity.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The Slow Luxury model implies accepting lower occupancy in exchange for higher ADR and a more selective guest demographic. Most luxury properties are "happy to maintain higher rates, even at the expense of occupancy", with suites going for higher rates than ever and quickly selling out while base-rate rooms remain difficult to fill. This pricing behaviour is not a problem to solve: it is the signal that the model is working. But it requires management teams and ownership structures that are prepared to resist conventional occupancy targets in favour of rate integrity.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
