285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 88 0 R
/T (Content strategy versus communication restraint.)
/E (Content strategy versus communication restraint.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The default instinct in most marketing teams is to communicate more. The Slow Luxury model inverts this logic: the operators whose brand equity is growing fastest are publishing less, not more. An emerging status symbol among the ultra-affluent is being genuinely unreachable, not tethered to constant digital stimulation. For a marketing team measured on impressions and follower count, this is a structurally difficult instruction to operationalise, and it requires a shared conviction, from ownership downward, that restraint is a long-term revenue strategy, not an abdication of marketing responsibility.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The operators who navigate all three tensions successfully are those who have aligned ownership, management, and brand strategy around a shared conviction that restraint is a long-term revenue strategy, not a temporary positioning experiment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
